expect: fail

# **every shape that takes no visibility modifier**, in one case, because they are one rule read from
# eight sides: a modifier says who may name a declaration, and each of these is either not a declaration
# or is already exactly as reachable as whatever owns it.
#
# what the case really pins is the recovery: each refusal lands on the modifier itself rather than on the
# declaration behind it, the declaration behind it still parses, and nothing cascades - so eight misplaced
# words cost eight diagnostics and not a truncated file. that only holds because
# Parser::parse_visibility_prefix *consumes* the token before refusing it, which is also what keeps the
# declaration pass and the body pass on the same token
#
# `internal` on a member used to live here. it is a real rung now - visibility/member_internal and
# errors/internal_member_across_modules are that case
--- OUT --->
[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:13:5

  'private' cannot be written here. A type declared inside another is only ever named through its owner, so it is already as reachable as that owner is.

  12 |     // a nested type is only ever named through its owner
  13 |     private struct Inner
     :     ^^^^^^^
  14 |     {

[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:19:5

  'private' cannot be written here. A destructor is never called by name - the compiler runs it where the value it belongs to ends - so there is no call site for a modifier to narrow.

  18 |     // a destructor is never called by name
  19 |     private destructor()
     :     ^^^^^^^
  20 |     {

[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:24:5

  'private' cannot be written here. A constant declared inside a type is reached through that type, so it is already as reachable as its owner is - and there is no narrower scope for one.

  23 |     // a constant declared inside a type is reached through that type
  24 |     private const int32 STEP = 2;
     :     ^^^^^^^
  25 | }

[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:28:1

  'private' cannot be written here. An operator's symbol is global wherever it is declared - one entry in one table that every module reads - so there is no scope for it to be narrowed to.

  27 | // an operator's symbol is global wherever it is written
  28 | private operator (Holder $a) + (Holder $b) : int32
     : ^^^^^^^
  29 | {

[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:36:5

  'private' cannot be written here. A method declared in an interface is a requirement, so it is reachable exactly where the interface is - it is what an implementor promises to answer.

  35 |     // a requirement *is* the interface's surface
  36 |     private function area() : int32;
     :     ^^^^^^^
  37 | }

[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:43:5

  'private' cannot be written here. A declaration inside a body is already reachable from that block and from nowhere else, so there is nothing for a modifier to narrow.

  42 |     // nowhere else already
  43 |     private struct Local
     :     ^^^^^^^
  44 |     {

[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:48:5

  'private' cannot be written here. A declaration inside a body is already reachable from that block and from nowhere else, so there is nothing for a modifier to narrow.

  47 | 
  48 |     private function nested() : int32
     :     ^^^^^^^
  49 |     {

[error] visibility_misplaced.eco:55:1

  'public' cannot be written here. A visibility modifier says who may name a declaration, and this is not one.

  54 | // nor on something that is not a declaration
  55 | public echo 1;
     : ^^^^^^
  56 | 

8 errors, nothing was compiled.
